{"name":"School Ink","hex":"#31373f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"school","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An institution dedicated to teaching and learning; an educational institution.","An educational institution providing primary and secondary education, prior to tertiary education (college or university)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To educate, teach, or train (often, but not necessarily, in a school).","To defeat emphatically, to teach an opponent a harsh lesson."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/school"},{"term":"ink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigment (or dye)-based fluid used for writing, printing etc.","A particular type, color or container of this fluid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply ink to; to cover or smear with ink.","To sign (a contract or similar document)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ink"}],"entries":[{"title":"School","blocks":[{"text":"A school is an educational institution designed to provide learning environments for the teaching of students, usually under the direction of teachers. Most countries have systems of formal education, which is sometimes compulsory. In these systems, students progress through a series of schools that can be built and operated by both government and private organizations. The names for these schools vary by country but generally include primary school for young children and secondary school for teenagers who have completed primary education. An institution where higher education is taught is commonly called a university college or university."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/%D0%A8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B0_%E2%84%962_%D0%B3._%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D1%8C%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0.jpg/330px-%D0%A8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B0_%E2%84%962_%D0%B3._%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D1%8C%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/School"},{"title":"Ink","blocks":[{"text":"Ink is a gel, sol, or solution that contains at least one colorant, such as a dye or pigment, and is used to color a surface to produce an image, text, or design. Ink is used for drawing or writing with a pen, brush, reed pen, or quill. Thicker inks, in paste form, are used extensively in letterpress and lithographic printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg/330px-F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/First_primary_school_building_in_Nigeria_in_Badagry%2C_Nigeria.jpg/500px-First_primary_school_building_in_Nigeria_in_Badagry%2C_Nigeria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/First_primary_school_building_in_Nigeria_in_Badagry%2C_Nigeria.jpg/1280px-First_primary_school_building_in_Nigeria_in_Badagry%2C_Nigeria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/First_primary_school_building_in_Nigeria_in_Badagry%2C_Nigeria.jpg/500px-First_primary_school_building_in_Nigeria_in_Badagry%2C_Nigeria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"First primary school in Nigeria, built in 1845[1] ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFirst_primary_school_building_in_Nigeria_in_Badagry%2C_Nigeria.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/1st_High_school_of_Argos%2C_Greece.jpg/500px-1st_High_school_of_Argos%2C_Greece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons